@startuml j5-staff-reply
!include style.iuml
title J5 A staff reply reaches the chat
actor Staff
participant "Staff page\n(staff/index.html,\nstaff/staff.js, sync.js)" as SP
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix
database "Store (Postgres)\nthrough api/_store.js" as Store
participant "api/messages.js" as Msg
participant "Patient chat\n(chat.js, sync.js, shared.js)" as Chat
actor Patient
autonumber

Staff -> SP : opens a ticket, types in the reply box and presses "Send reply"
SP -> Core : FD.replyToTicket (ticket, text)
Core --> SP : the reply is on the ticket in the staff browser;\n"Needs human" or "Urgent" becomes "Answered"
SP --> Staff : "Sent. The patient sees it in their chat."
SP -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets (the ticket, with the desk code)
Tix -> Store : merged into the row in the table tickets:\nevery staff reply kept, the status further along wins
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets?patient=<id> (with this browser's key)
Tix -> Store : read this patient's tickets
Tix --> Chat : the ticket with the staff reply
Chat -> Chat : sync.js merges it into this browser's tickets; chat.js redraws
Chat --> Patient : the reply, headed "From the clinic team"
Chat -> Msg : shared.js: POST /api/messages (the staff reply, once)
Msg -> Store : a row in the table messages
@enduml
